== Really, an oscilloscope?

An oscilloscope seems like a strange choice for a display technology, but there really weren't other choices.

Televisions existed, but generating a TV frame from something other than a recording would have required specialized hardware that didn't exist yet.

Therefore, an oscilloscope that could draw a little dot based on an input voltage was perfect.

The net, ground, and paddles were just a "dot" that was swept over a line. The "ghosting" made a solid-ish line.

